# #75: /ttl life1 status <player> <preset> jumps a Life 1 soul to a karma tier (karma/life1_status.js, karma.toml
# [presets]); /ttl life1 days sets the days of active play (the Legend's 30, which idle time and tick speed never give);
# /ttl life1 trial sets the Trial of the Soul's result in the Corridor. Expect no "ttl:" failure lines. The command itself
# fails with "ttl: ..." when a preset no longer reaches its tier.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLifeA
@sleep 4
ttl life1 status TtlBotLifeA
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect tier underdog
ttl life1 status TtlBotLifeA legendary
ttl ops expect cmdlog last "ttl life1 status"
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect tier legendary
ttl life1 status TtlBotLifeA dark
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect tier normal
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect dark true
ttl life1 status TtlBotLifeA elite
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect tier elite
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect dark false
ttl life1 days TtlBotLifeA 40
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect days 40
ttl life1 days TtlBotLifeA 30
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect days 30
ttl life1 status TtlBotLifeA
# The Corridor judges the staff-set life like any other: a Hero gets the Hero's offers.
kill TtlBotLifeA
@sleep 1
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect phase corridor
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect tier elite
ttl karma TtlBotLifeA expect offers 4
ttl reset TtlBotLifeA
ttlbot remove TtlBotLifeA
# The Trial gate: an underdog draws its unique at random; with the Trial set to passed it picks 1 of 3 (step unique).
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLifeB
@sleep 4
kill TtlBotLifeB
execute as TtlBotLifeB run ttl wish strength
ttl life1 trial TtlBotLifeB pass
ttl life1 status TtlBotLifeB
ttl karma TtlBotLifeB expect tier underdog
execute as TtlBotLifeB run ttl choose slime
@sleep 1
ttl karma TtlBotLifeB expect step unique
ttl karma TtlBotLifeB pick
ttl karma TtlBotLifeB expect phase life2
ttl reset TtlBotLifeB
ttlbot remove TtlBotLifeB
